<title>ITALY: Italy's IRI moves on Autostrade.</title>
<headline>Italy's IRI moves on Autostrade.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian state industrial holding IRI on Thursday said it had approved a share transfer that will give it control of almost all stock in motorway operator Autostrade prior to the company's sell-off, planned to take place by June.</p>
<p>A statement said an IRI shareholders' meeting had approved the transfer of 66.2 percent of Autostrade now held by IRI unit Fintecna to IRI itself.</p>
<p>The operation will take IRI's stake in Autostrade to 87 percent and will allow proceeds from the sale to flow directly to IRI to help reduce its debts.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom +39 6 6782505</p>
</text>
